<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61164" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύ̄φ-ων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυφός</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>crooked piece of wood, bent yoke
				of the plough</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				1201
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύφωνες, οἱ</span>, <i>two bars</i> in the frame of a chariot,
				<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				1.143
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>pillory</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τῷ κ. αὐχένα ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cratin.
					115
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				476
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				606
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεθῆναι ἐν τῷ κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1306b2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαστιγούσθω ἐν τῷ κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>OGI</u>
					483.177
				</span></i>
			 (Pergam.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>one who has had his neck in the pillory, knave</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				178
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Pseudol.</u>
				17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> part of a
			woman's dress, <i><span class="en">
				Posidipp.
				44
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> Archit.,
				<i>curved beam,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				42(1).102.224
			</span></i>, al. (Epid., <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>V.</b> part of a water-wheel, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLond.</u>
				3.1177.213
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
